/* ===== Skin tokens =====
   Every skin-dependent color reads a --sasq-* variable with the ORIGINAL dark literal as its
   fallback. The variables are defined per-skin in SasquatchWidgetThemeDark.uss /
   SasquatchWidgetThemeLight.uss (loaded onto the build root by LayoutTreeBuilder next to the
   sasq-skin-dark / sasq-skin-light class). Hosts that load only THIS sheet (Welcome, Tutorial,
   Showcase, Feedback, SpringSandbox chrome) resolve the fallbacks — i.e. the historical dark
   look, byte-for-byte. Skin-NEUTRAL colors stay literal on purpose: validation reds/ambers,
   white text/knobs sitting on accent fills, overlays drawn over images or color swatches, and
   the black bottom hairlines. NOTE: USS variables don't work in shorthand properties, so
   border colors that carry a variable are written as the four longhands. */

/* Label-above-field (opt-in per binding, and the fallback FieldLabelColumn stacks a too-narrow track to):
   put the field's label on its own line above the rest of the row instead of in the inspector's left label
   column. Applies to BaseField widgets and PropertyField-wrapped fields (the inner base-field is the row).

   Done by WRAPPING the row and giving the label a full-width first line — NOT by flipping the row to a
   column. A column stacks EVERY child, and a composite widget's row is not just [label][input]: a
   MinMaxSlider mounts [label][min][track][max] and a Slider with its value field on the Left mounts
   [label][value][track], so the column put one part per line — a 20px min-max row measured 74px with the
   min value above the track above the max. Wrapping leaves those parts side by side on line two, exactly
   where they were, and is identical to a column for the ordinary [label][input] row. */
.sasq-label-above.unity-base-field,
.sasq-label-above > .unity-base-field {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: stretch;
}
/* Scoped to the row's OWN label and input. A descendant selector also reaches a composite's inner value
   fields (a MinMaxSlider's min/max FloatFields are base fields in their own right), and a 100%-wide inner
   label would re-break the very row this is meant to fix. */
.sasq-label-above.unity-base-field > .unity-base-field__label,
.sasq-label-above > .unity-base-field > .unity-base-field__label {
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: none;
    width: 100%;
    flex-basis: 100%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    -unity-text-align: middle-left;
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-bottom: 1px;
}
.sasq-label-above.unity-base-field > .unity-base-field__input,
.sasq-label-above > .unity-base-field > .unity-base-field__input {
    flex-grow: 1;
}

/* A composite field's number boxes take their width from the ROW, never from their own text.

   Unity ships this container as `flex-shrink: 0` with `flex-basis: auto`, and an auto basis on a row child
   is MEASURED FROM ITS CONTENT — so typing a long value made the container size itself to the digits and
   then refuse to give the width back. Measured in a 320px lane with "-1234567890.123456" in every box:

       Vector2 304   Vector3 452   Vector4 604   Rect 304   Bounds 452   (available: 192)

   The row genuinely painted past the inspector edge, which is what summoned HorizontalOverflowRescue's pan
   rail. Every composite was affected — Vector2/3/4, Vector2Int/3Int, Rect, RectInt, Bounds, BoundsInt and
   the Quaternion euler row — with or without a prefix/suffix; affixes only made it wider sooner. Scalar
   fields were never affected, because their width is cross-axis and basis never gets a vote.

   Basis 0 + shrink 1 + min-width 0 says "the row decides", which is what every other inspector row already
   does. The digits that no longer fit are clipped by the stock text input, exactly as they are in Unity's
   own Transform. A USS rule rather than a build-time walk on purpose: a PropertyField builds its real
   field during BIND, a tick after the build pass, so a walk would need the same re-arm dance the affixes
   carry — a stylesheet just applies whenever the element shows up.

   Scoped by attachment, not by selector: LayoutTreeBuilder adds this sheet to the build root, so it reaches
   Sasquatch-built trees (both live render paths) and nothing else in the editor. */
.unity-composite-field__input {
    flex-shrink: 1;
    flex-basis: 0;
    min-width: 0;
}

/* Toggle-as-switch track */
.sq-toggle .unity-toggle__input {
    background-color: var(--sasq-control-bg, #2b2b2b);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-width: 1px;
    width: 44px;
    height: 20px;
    max-height: 20px;
    min-height: 20px;
    flex-grow: 0;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    position: relative;
}

/* Switch knob */
.sq-toggle .unity-toggle__checkmark {
    background-image: none;
    background-color: var(--sasq-knob, #a0a0a0);
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    border-width: 0px;
    position: absolute;
    left: 2px;
    top: 2px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    transition-property: left, background-color;
    transition-duration: 0.15s;
}

/* NOTE: the `left` half of that transition is a FALLBACK, not the shipping behaviour. Every switch the
   package builds runs EditorSpringFX.SpringToggleKnob, which rewrites this element's transition list inline
   (background-color only) and THROWS the knob across on a spring instead — a transition cannot overshoot,
   and the overshoot is the whole point. The rule stays so a `.sq-toggle` that never reaches that call still
   slides rather than teleports; to change how a switch feels, change the spring, not this line. */

/* Suppress the slide transition on freshly-built toggles (applied for one frame on each
   rebuild) so the intro animation doesn't replay when an unrelated value changes. */
.sq-toggle--instant .unity-toggle__checkmark,
.sq-toggle--instant .unity-toggle__input {
    transition-duration: 0s;
}

/* Hover feedback — subtle lift on the track + knob so the switch doesn't feel static.
   Applies in the designer and in live inspectors (both load this stylesheet). */
.sq-toggle:hover .unity-toggle__input {
    background-color: var(--sasq-control-bg-hover, #353535);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border-hover, #5a5a5a);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border-hover, #5a5a5a);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border-hover, #5a5a5a);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border-hover, #5a5a5a);
}
.sq-toggle:hover .unity-toggle__checkmark {
    background-color: var(--sasq-knob-hover, #c0c0c0);
}
.sq-toggle:checked:hover .unity-toggle__input {
    background-color: var(--sasq-toggle-on-hover, #264a82);
    /* keep a clearly darker outline even while hovering the ON state */
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-toggle-on-hover-border, #16304f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-toggle-on-hover-border, #16304f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-toggle-on-hover-border, #16304f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-toggle-on-hover-border, #16304f);
}
.sq-toggle:checked:hover .unity-toggle__checkmark {
    background-color: #ffffff;
}

/* Checked states */
.sq-toggle:checked .unity-toggle__input {
    background-color: var(--sasq-toggle-on, #1e3d6b); /* Default accent (overridden inline if customized) */
    /* A near-black border so the ON edge reads clearly against the blue fill (the grey #3f3f3f default
       blurred into the blue — a problem for low-contrast / color-blind viewers). Color only; width stays 1px. */
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-toggle-on-border, #5C5C5C);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-toggle-on-border, #5C5C5C);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-toggle-on-border, #5C5C5C);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-toggle-on-border, #5C5C5C);
}

.sq-toggle:checked .unity-toggle__checkmark {
    left: 26px; /* width 44 - knob 14 - margin 2 - border 2 */
    background-color: #ffffff;
}

/* Switch variants */
.sq-toggle--rounded .unity-toggle__input {
    border-radius: 10px;
}
.sq-toggle--rounded .unity-toggle__checkmark {
    border-radius: 7px;
}

.sq-toggle--square .unity-toggle__input {
    border-radius: 2px;
}
.sq-toggle--square .unity-toggle__checkmark {
    border-radius: 1px;
}

.sq-toggle--slim .unity-toggle__input {
    height: 10px;
    max-height: 10px;
    min-height: 10px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    /* The knob is intentionally taller than the 10px track (a protruding "switch" look). The track's
       layout box only reserves margin-top + height, so without a bottom margin the row collapses to 15px
       and the knob's lower edge (~y17) gets clipped. Reserve a full 20px row (5 + 10 + 5) — matching a
       normal toggle, which also keeps row heights consistent — so the knob shows in full. */
    margin-top: 5px;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
    width: 44px;
    overflow: visible;
}
.sq-toggle--slim .unity-toggle__checkmark {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    top: -4px; /* knob sits a hair above the track center for visual balance (row-y 1→17 in the 20px row) */
    left: 0px;
}
.sq-toggle--slim:checked .unity-toggle__checkmark {
    left: 26px;
}

/* ON/OFF Overlay Text styling */
.sq-toggle-onoff-label {
    position: absolute;
    color: var(--sasq-text-faint, #888888);
    font-size: 10px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    top: 50%;
    translate: 0 -50%;
    /* OFF state: text sits on the right, opposite the left knob. "OFF" (3 chars) is wider than the
       "ON" it flips to (see :checked below), so a symmetric 6px inset let the wider word's LEFT edge
       reach back and touch the knob — most visible on Extra Large, which scales the whole switch from
       its left edge. A smaller inset nudges "OFF" clear of the knob; the right side is empty when off. */
    right: 3px;
}

.sq-toggle:checked .sq-toggle-onoff-label {
    left: 6px;
    right: auto;
    /* FALLBACK ONLY, and only correct for the default blue track. Every switch BindingFactory builds writes
       this color inline from the track's ACTUAL fill (BindingFactory.Toggle → ApplyOnOffInk), because a light
       custom fill — yellow, a pastel accent — leaves white "ON" unreadable. The rule stays for the toggles
       that never reach that call (the spring sandbox). To change how the word reads, change ApplyOnOffInk. */
    color: #ffffff;
}

/* Custom Sizes */
.sq-size--compact {
    font-size: 10px;
}
.sq-size--compact .unity-label {
    font-size: 10px;
}
.sq-size--compact .unity-text-element {
    font-size: 10px;
}
.sq-size--compact .unity-base-field__input {
    height: 16px;
    min-height: 16px;
    font-size: 10px;
}

.sq-size--large {
    font-size: 14px;
}
.sq-size--large .unity-label {
    font-size: 14px;
}
.sq-size--large .unity-text-element {
    font-size: 14px;
}
.sq-size--large .unity-base-field__input {
    height: 26px;
    min-height: 26px;
    font-size: 14px;
}

/* Table column resize handle — the horizontal-resize cursor signals it's draggable.
   (Inline code can't set a system cursor; USS keywords can.) */
.sasq-col-resizer {
    cursor: resize-horizontal;
}

/* ---- Large-collection ergonomics: pagination toolbar, sort note, clickable Table headers ---- */

/* Clickable Table column header (label + sort glyph) — pointer cursor hints it sorts. */
.sasq-table-col-header:hover .unity-label {
    color: var(--sasq-colhead-hover, #EBEBEB);
}
/* The link cursor belongs to the ARROWS, not the whole header. Sorting used to be a click anywhere on the
   cell; it is now the glyph alone, so that the header's own surface is free for the reorder grip. A cell
   that still claimed "clickable" everywhere would be promising a sort it no longer performs. */
.sasq-col-sort-glyph {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--sasq-accent-text, #99C7FF);
    cursor: link;
}

/* ===== Live column reorder (TableColumnGrip) =====
   Hover a column header and a grip springs in on its left while the header text slides right to make room;
   drag it and the real columns rearrange in real time. Both halves are driven in C# — the lane is a spring
   on the label's padding, the grip's pop is a scale spring, the columns glide on translate springs — so
   only the paint lives here.

   The grip's own mark is a PAINTED GripGlyph, not a text character and not a background: it was a Braille
   "⠿" and drew nothing at all, because the editor font has no such glyph. Its colour lives in C# with the
   rest of that glyph's tinting. */

/* The header of the column being dragged. A soft accent wash, NOT a fade: the column is travelling under
   the user's hand and needs to read as lifted, not as removed. */
.sasq-col-grip-dragging {
    background-color: var(--sasq-accent-soft, rgba(46, 122, 217, 0.12));
}

/* Prev/Next pagination toolbar. */
.sasq-collection-pager {
    margin-top: 3px;
    margin-bottom: 3px;
}
.sasq-pager-btn {
    padding-left: 8px;
    padding-right: 8px;
    margin-left: 1px;
    margin-right: 1px;
    font-size: 11px;
}
.sasq-pager-label {
    margin-left: 4px;
    margin-right: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
}
.sasq-pager-count {
    margin-left: 6px;
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--sasq-pager-count, #999999);
}

/* iOS-style page dots (PaginationDisplayStyle.DotsOnly / ButtonsAndDots). The current page's dot is larger
   and accent-blue; the rest are small + muted. Clickable: each jumps straight to its page. */
.sasq-pager-dots {
    margin-left: 6px;
    margin-right: 6px;
}
.sasq-pager-dot {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin-left: 3px;
    margin-right: 3px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-pager-dot, rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.55));
}
.sasq-pager-dot:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-pager-dot-hover, rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.85));
}
.sasq-pager-dot.active {
    width: 11px;
    height: 11px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-pager-active, #4582ED);
}
.sasq-pager-dot-gap {
    font-size: 11px;
    margin-left: 2px;
    margin-right: 2px;
    color: var(--sasq-pager-gap, rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.7));
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}

/* List-mode sort dropdown row. */
.sasq-collection-sort {
    margin-right: 4px;
}

/* "Sorted by X ▲ · reorder paused [clear]" note. */
.sasq-collection-sortnote {
    margin-top: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
}
.sasq-sortnote-label {
    font-size: 10px;
    -unity-font-style: italic;
    color: var(--sasq-accent-text, #99C7FF);
}
.sasq-sortnote-clear {
    margin-left: 6px;
    padding-left: 6px;
    padding-right: 6px;
    font-size: 10px;
}

/* Resizable text-box bottom edge — vertical-resize cursor. */
.sasq-text-resizer {
    cursor: resize-vertical;
}

/* Rows container row-height resize handle — vertical-resize cursor signals it's draggable. */
.sasq-row-resizer {
    cursor: resize-vertical;
}

/* Validation and conditional warning highlight outline */
.sasq-binding-row,
.sasq-validation-wrapper {
    min-width: 0;
    flex-shrink: 1;
    align-self: stretch;
}

/* ===== Right-edge (and left-label) normalization =====
   Every full-width inspector row should reach the SAME right edge — "put a ruler on the far right and
   nothing wobbles". NormalizeFullRowBinding zeroes the OUTER row element's horizontal margins, but some
   widgets wrap the real field one level deeper, where that pass can't reach it:
     • DisplayType.Default          → the field sits inside a PropertyField wrapper
     • a custom widget with [Header]→ the field sits inside WrapWithHeader's column
   The nested Unity field keeps the editor theme's default ~3px horizontal field margin, so its input (and
   its label) stop ~3px short of the row edge — and only for SOME widgets, which is exactly the misalignment.
   Zero that nested margin. The child combinator keeps it surgical: composite sub-fields (e.g. a Vector2's
   x/y) and a slider's trailing value field are NOT direct children of the row or the property field, so
   they keep their own spacing (synthetic right-edge spread measured 3px -> 0px). */
.sasq-binding-row > .unity-base-field,
.sasq-binding-row .unity-property-field > .unity-base-field {
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 0;
}

/* The Min-Max slider's drag groove carries a built-in 1px right margin, so its track stops 1px shy of the
   row edge while every other slider reaches it. */
.sasq-binding-row .unity-min-max-slider__tracker {
    margin-right: 0;
}

/* ===== Slider knobs are OPAQUE =====
   The editor theme paints the slider thumb at 50% alpha (measured: a #999999 thumb composites to 95/255
   over the #262626 field and 109/255 over the #424242 track), so the track reads straight through the
   knob as a brighter band across its middle. Repaint it solid.

   The hover rule deliberately mirrors the theme's OWN selector shape (state on the slider, not the
   dragger) so the two tie on specificity — this sheet is attached to the element and resolves after the
   panel's default theme, so a tie goes to us. Without it, hovering would hand the knob back to the
   translucent thumb color.

   Read-only does NOT ride this rule: SetEnabled(false) dims via opacity on the field root, and UITK
   composites that per element down the subtree, which puts the see-through knob straight back. Those
   sliders are dimmed in COLOUR instead, inline, by BindingFactory.ApplyReadOnlySliderLook. A user-picked
   Knob Color is likewise applied INLINE by BindingFactory.ApplySliderLook and still wins.
   Covers Slider, SliderInt and the per-axis Vector Sliders (all real BaseSliders); the Min-Max thumbs
   are the same thumb part under their own class names. The min-max CENTER BAR is deliberately absent —
   that one is a fill spanning the selected range, not a knob. */
.unity-base-slider__dragger,
.unity-min-max-slider__min-thumb,
.unity-min-max-slider__max-thumb {
    background-color: var(--sasq-slider-knob, #999999);
}

.unity-base-slider:hover:enabled .unity-base-slider__dragger,
.unity-min-max-slider:hover:enabled .unity-min-max-slider__min-thumb,
.unity-min-max-slider:hover:enabled .unity-min-max-slider__max-thumb {
    background-color: var(--sasq-slider-knob-hover, #b4b4b4);
}

.sasq-warning-highlight {
    border-color: #ef4444 !important;
    border-width: 1px !important;
}

/* ===== Condition Debugger overlay & card ===== */
/* The reveal-in-place wash drawn over a field that conditions would hide/disable. Absolute inset-0 + pickable
   (set in C#) so it both blocks editing of the revealed field and drives the hover card. */
.sasq-cond-debug-overlay {
    border-width: 2px;
    border-top-left-radius: 4px;
    border-top-right-radius: 4px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;
}
.sasq-cond-debug-hidden {
    background-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.42);
    border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.95);
}
.sasq-cond-debug-disabled {
    background-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.34);
    border-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.95);
}

/* Corner verdict pill (HIDDEN / DISABLED). */
.sasq-cond-debug-pill {
    position: absolute;
    top: 2px;
    right: 2px;
    padding-left: 5px;
    padding-right: 5px;
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    font-size: 10px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    color: rgb(255, 255, 255);
    border-top-left-radius: 3px;
    border-top-right-radius: 3px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 3px;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 3px;
}
.sasq-cond-debug-hidden .sasq-cond-debug-pill { background-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.95); }
.sasq-cond-debug-disabled .sasq-cond-debug-pill { background-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.95); }

/* The floating breakdown card shown on hover (appended to the build root, absolute, on top). */
.sasq-cond-card {
    max-width: 340px;
    padding-left: 10px;
    padding-right: 10px;
    padding-top: 8px;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-popup-bg, rgba(28, 30, 34, 0.98));
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-popup-border, rgba(120, 130, 145, 0.55));
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-popup-border, rgba(120, 130, 145, 0.55));
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-popup-border, rgba(120, 130, 145, 0.55));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-popup-border, rgba(120, 130, 145, 0.55));
    border-top-left-radius: 6px;
    border-top-right-radius: 6px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 6px;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 6px;
}
.sasq-cond-card-title {
    font-size: 11px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
}
.sasq-cond-card-title--hidden { color: var(--sasq-danger-fg, rgb(248, 113, 113)); }
.sasq-cond-card-title--disabled { color: var(--sasq-warn-fg, rgb(251, 191, 36)); }
.sasq-cond-group-label {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--sasq-popup-text-soft, rgba(180, 188, 200, 0.85));
    margin-top: 3px;
    margin-bottom: 1px;
}
.sasq-cond-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 1px;
    margin-bottom: 1px;
}
.sasq-cond-chip {
    font-size: 10px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    color: rgb(255, 255, 255);
    padding-left: 4px;
    padding-right: 4px;
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    margin-right: 6px;
    border-top-left-radius: 3px;
    border-top-right-radius: 3px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 3px;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 3px;
}
.sasq-cond-chip-pass { background-color: rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.92); }
.sasq-cond-chip-fail { background-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.92); }
.sasq-cond-rule {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--sasq-popup-text, rgb(224, 228, 234));
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-shrink: 1;
}
.sasq-cond-actual {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--sasq-popup-text-faint, rgba(160, 168, 180, 0.9));
    margin-left: 6px;
}
.sasq-cond-divider {
    height: 1px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-popup-divider, rgba(120, 130, 145, 0.4));
    margin-top: 6px;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
}
.sasq-cond-headline {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--sasq-popup-headline, rgba(205, 212, 222, 0.95));
    white-space: normal;
}

/* Empty column/row drop slot shown in design mode for a container with an explicit track count, so an
   empty N-column container visibly shows N droppable cells. Purely a visual affordance (the slot ignores
   picking so drops fall through to the parent container). */
.sasq-drop-slot {
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-drop-slot-border, rgba(120, 120, 120, 0.5));
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-drop-slot-border, rgba(120, 120, 120, 0.5));
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-drop-slot-border, rgba(120, 120, 120, 0.5));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-drop-slot-border, rgba(120, 120, 120, 0.5));
    border-top-left-radius: 4px;
    border-top-right-radius: 4px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-drop-slot-bg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.031));
    font-size: 16px;
}

/* Progress Bar Track */
.sasq-progress-track {
    background-color: var(--sasq-control-bg, #2b2b2b);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    height: 20px;
    min-height: 20px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-top: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
}

/* Progress Bar Fill. The background-color here is only a fallback — the widget always sets the
   resolved fill inline (BindingFactory.ProgressFillDefault); keep the two in sync. The rounded
   corners give the leading edge a soft cap inside the radius-4 track, and the 1px translucent
   top border reads as a highlight sheen at any DPI scale (a single border scales cleanly at
   125%/150%, unlike stacked hairline divs). */
.sasq-progress-fill {
    background-color: var(--sasq-progress-fill, #2E7AD9);
    height: 100%;
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border-top-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16);
}

/* Progress Bar readout. Two perfectly-aligned copies of the text: this base copy spans the whole
   track, and a second copy (--fill, below) rides inside an invisible clip whose width mirrors the
   fill — so the readout inverts color exactly at the fill's leading edge. Each copy's color is
   picked in code for contrast against ITS backdrop (fill / track / per-value gradient), which is
   what keeps these small glyphs crisp: no outline or shadow smearing them. */
.sasq-progress-label {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    color: #f4f4f4;
    font-size: 11px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
}

/* The fill-side copy. Color is set inline per resolved fill; this is only the pre-layout fallback. */
.sasq-progress-label--fill {
    color: #ffffff;
}

/* Invisible clip carrying the fill-side copy; its width is driven in lockstep with the fill. */
.sasq-progress-label-clip {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
}

/* Optional Text Backdrop (accessibility): full-track centering host + an auto-sized pill behind a
   single readout copy — guaranteed contrast regardless of bar colors, in either editor skin. */
.sasq-progress-backdrop-host {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}

.sasq-progress-label-backdrop {
    max-width: 100%;
    background-color: rgba(10, 10, 10, 0.62);
    border-radius: 8px;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    padding: 1px 7px;
}

/* Readout copy riding the pill: back in flow, auto-sized, always light-on-dark. */
.sasq-progress-label--boxed {
    position: relative;
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
    color: #ffffff;
}

/* Expandable Help Box Header */
.sasq-help-expand-header {
    background-color: var(--sasq-pane-header-bg, #2d2d2d);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-left-radius: 4px;
    border-top-right-radius: 4px;
    padding: 6px 10px;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
}
.sasq-help-expand-header:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-header-bg, #383838);
}

/* Chevron */
.sasq-help-expand-chevron {
    margin-right: 6px;
    color: var(--sasq-chevron, #5d5d5d);
    font-size: 10px;
    width: 14px;
}

/* Details pane */
.sasq-help-expand-details {
    background-color: var(--sasq-pane-bg, #222222);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-width: 0 1px 1px 1px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-help, #cccccc);
}

/* Asset Preview Thumbnail Container */
.sasq-asset-preview-container {
    background-color: var(--sasq-well-bg, #1e1e1e);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 2px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    overflow: hidden;
}

.sasq-asset-preview-image {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 2px;
}

/* Reset-view button overlaid on the interactive asset preview (bottom-left corner). Sits over the
   rendered preview image, so its scrim colors are skin-neutral by design. */
.sasq-asset-preview-reset {
    position: absolute;
    left: 3px;
    bottom: 3px;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18);
    border-radius: 4px;
}
.sasq-asset-preview-reset:hover {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
}

/* 2D/3D toggle overlaid on the interactive asset preview (bottom-right corner). The ON (blue) background is
   set inline by the widget; OFF falls back to this neutral-dark pill (over the image — skin-neutral). */
.sasq-asset-preview-2d {
    position: absolute;
    right: 3px;
    bottom: 3px;
    height: 18px;
    padding-left: 5px;
    padding-right: 5px;
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 10px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25);
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
}
.sasq-asset-preview-2d:hover {
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
}

.sasq-progress-interactive {
    cursor: link;
}

/* ===== Audio Preview widget ===== */
/* Waveform display area (Show Soundwaves mode) */
.sasq-audio-waveform {
    background-color: var(--sasq-well-bg, #1e1e1e);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
}

/* Thin vertical playhead that slides across the field / waveform during playback */
.sasq-audio-playhead {
    background-color: var(--sasq-playhead, #e0b020);
    width: 2px;
}

/* Interactive (scrubbable) waveform */
.sasq-audio-interactive {
    cursor: link;
}

/* Clickable elements */
.sasq-clickable {
    cursor: link;
}

/* Markdown help-box hyperlink — class is toggled on only while the pointer is over a <link> span,
   so the hand cursor appears exactly over the link text (a HelpBox label has no per-span cursor). */
.sasq-md-link-hover {
    cursor: link;
}

/* ===== Toggle Group (Particle-System-style collapsible group; the bound bool IS the header checkbox) ===== */
.sasq-group {
    margin-top: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
}

/* Header bar — the entire bar is the clickable expand/collapse surface. */
.sasq-group-header {
    background-color: var(--sasq-header-bg, #383838);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-left-radius: 4px;
    border-top-right-radius: 4px;
    /* Left pad is 5, not 6, so the title lands on LayoutTreeBuilder.SectionGutter (18px) exactly like a Card's
       and a Foldout's: 1px border + 5px pad + 10px chevron + 2px chevron gap = 18. Every caller builds the
       chevron at size 10 (SasquatchIcons.Create), which is why .sasq-group-chevron declares 10 below — change
       either number and this arithmetic has to move with it. Pinned by TestContainerTitlesShareTwoLeftEdges. */
    padding: 4px 6px 4px 5px;
    cursor: link;
}
.sasq-group-header:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-header-bg-hover, #424242);
}

/* Left-pinned expand indicator. 10px + the 2px gap IS the header's title gutter (see above); every builder
   also passes 10 inline to SasquatchIcons.Create, so the two agree rather than the USS being dead weight. */
.sasq-group-chevron {
    color: var(--sasq-chevron, #5d5d5d);
    font-size: 10px;
    width: 10px;
    margin-right: 2px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}

/* Group name. Its own token rather than the shared --sasq-text-title, so container titles can carry one ink
   (LayoutTreeBuilder.TitleInk) without dragging the palette window and the UnityEvent captions along. */
.sasq-group-title {
    color: var(--sasq-text-node-title, #e6e6e6);
    -unity-font-style: bold;
}

/* Bound checkbox — kept as a plain checkbox (like a particle-system module's enable box). Hide the empty
   BaseField label column and stop the input from growing so it sits flush next to the name. */
.sasq-group-toggle {
    margin: 0 5px 0 0;
    flex-grow: 0;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}
.sasq-group-toggle .unity-base-field__label {
    display: none;
    min-width: 0;
    width: 0;
}
.sasq-group-toggle .unity-toggle__input {
    flex-grow: 0;
}

/* Content area — inset under the header; Unity greys it automatically when SetEnabled(false). */
.sasq-group-content {
    background-color: var(--sasq-group-content-bg, #2b2b2b);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-width: 0 1px 1px 1px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;
    /* Left pad 17 (+ the 1px border) puts the body on the same 18px gutter as the header's title, so the
       fields hang under the name rather than under the caret — the rule the --list variant below already
       followed. The other three sides keep the original 6/8 box inset. */
    padding: 6px 8px 6px 17px;
}

/* ===== List row style (Project Settings ▸ Sasquatch Inspector ▸ Expandable Rows = List) =====
   The same shell with the per-row box removed: no border, no fill, no radius, no margin. A run of expandable
   widgets then reads as ONE list rather than N stacked cards, and neighbours are parted by a hairline instead
   of a gap. Scoped to this modifier so container groups, the Welcome window, the palette editor and the spring
   sandbox (the other .sasq-group users) keep the card look. Applied only by BuildExpandableGroup. */
.sasq-group--list {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0;
}
.sasq-group--list > .sasq-group-header {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-width: 0;
    border-top-left-radius: 0;
    border-top-right-radius: 0;
    /* Left pad stays 6 (not the boxed shell's 5) because this variant drops the 1px border — 6 + 10 + 2 is
       the same 18px title gutter. */
    padding: 2px 6px;
}
/* Same specificity as the base :hover rule and declared later, so it must be restated to survive. Row hover
   is the only chrome a list row has left — it is what tells you the whole bar is the click target. */
.sasq-group--list > .sasq-group-header:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-header-bg-hover, #424242);
}
.sasq-group--list > .sasq-group-content {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-width: 0;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 0;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 0;
    /* Left pad clears the chevron so expanded content hangs under the title, not under the caret — 18 exactly,
       the shared section gutter (no border to subtract on this variant). */
    padding: 2px 6px 6px 18px;
}
/* Drawn only while another list row follows (BindingFactory.AttachListRowRule) — a trailing rule under the
   last row of a run reads as "there's more below". */
.sasq-group--list-rule {
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-row-divider, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1));
    border-bottom-width: 1px;
}

/* Unbound-field sync banner (NotificationBanner mode): slim accent-tinted row at the top of the
   real inspector offering to add fields that exist in code but not in the layout. The blue tint
   washes are skin-neutral; only the texts flip. */
.sasq-sync-banner {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    background-color: rgba(53, 96, 160, 0.18);
    border-color: rgba(70, 120, 190, 0.55);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    margin: 2px 4px 4px 4px;
}

.sasq-sync-banner__label {
    flex-grow: 1;
    color: var(--sasq-banner-fg, #c9d6e8);
    white-space: normal;
}

.sasq-sync-banner__btn {
    margin-left: 8px;
    padding: 2px 10px;
}

/* Borderless × so dismissal reads as quiet, not destructive. */
.sasq-sync-banner__dismiss {
    margin-left: 4px;
    padding: 0 6px;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-width: 0;
    color: var(--sasq-banner-dismiss, #9fb0c4);
}

.sasq-sync-banner__dismiss:hover {
    color: var(--sasq-text-strong, #ffffff);
}

/* Designer stand-in for a binding whose property no longer exists in code (deleted/renamed while
   auto-sync hasn't run). The real inspector hides dead bindings entirely; the designer shows this
   red-tinted row so the stale node stays discoverable, selectable and deletable. */
.sasq-missing-binding {
    background-color: rgba(190, 60, 60, 0.15);
    border-color: rgba(220, 90, 90, 0.8);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    margin: 1px 0;
}

.sasq-missing-binding .unity-label {
    color: var(--sasq-missing-fg, #e08585);
}

/* Guidance card for a plain Dictionary<,> binding: the field exists in code but Unity can't serialize
   it, so there is no SerializedProperty to draw or save. Informational (not an error like the red
   missing-binding row): a HelpBox explaining why, plus a click-to-copy SerializedDictionary declaration. */
.sasq-unserializable-dict {
    padding: 2px 0;
    margin: 1px 0;
}

.sasq-unserializable-dict__code {
    font-size: 11px;
    padding: 3px 6px;
    margin-right: 4px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background-color: rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.35);
    white-space: normal;
}

/* The card's live-mode "Don't show this again" opt-out: a quiet link-style button, right-aligned,
   deliberately dimmer than the Copy action so it never competes with the actual guidance. */
.sasq-unserializable-dict__dismiss {
    font-size: 10px;
    padding: 1px 4px;
    margin: 1px 0 0 0;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-width: 0;
    color: rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.9);
}

.sasq-unserializable-dict__dismiss:hover {
    color: var(--sasq-text-muted, #9a9a9a);
}

/* Sibling rows uniform backgrounds & clean bottom borders.
   The divider color is a theme token rather than the old hardcoded black alpha, which sank into the
   group-content background on dark and muddied the light skin. Widths/last-row suppression are set per
   row in C# (LayoutTreeBuilder.ApplyRowSeparator) because they depend on the node's RowSeparator and on
   which row is last in the current page. */
.sasq-table-row {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-015, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.015));
    border-bottom-width: 1px;
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-row-divider, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1));
}

/* A table shows many rows at once, and a per-row ✕ / ▲ / ▼ is noise on every row you are NOT working on —
   a column of delete buttons reads as chrome competing with the data. Same opacity reveal the UnityEvent
   card's clear-✕ uses (.sasq-uevent-clear): faded out until the pointer is on the row.
   OPACITY, not display/visibility, on purpose — the lane keeps its width either way, so nothing reflows
   when a row is hovered and the columns never twitch as the pointer travels down the table. The buttons
   stay hit-testable while faded, which is harmless: reaching one with the pointer is what reveals it. */
.sasq-table-row-action {
    opacity: 0;
    transition-property: opacity;
    transition-duration: 0.12s;
}
.sasq-table-row:hover .sasq-table-row-action {
    opacity: 1;
}

.sasq-list-row {
    background-color: var(--sasq-list-row-bg, rgba(46, 46, 46, 0.22));
    border-bottom-width: 1px;
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-row-divider, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1));
}

/* Card separator: each row is its own tray. The left rail is what makes this work on TALL rows —
   a bottom hairline is a fixed 1px of signal no matter how far apart the boundaries are, while the
   rail grows with the row. Geometry (widths, padding, spacing) is applied in C# alongside it. */
.sasq-list-row--card {
    background-color: var(--sasq-row-card-bg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.045));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-row-rail, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2));
    border-bottom-width: 0;
}

/* ===== Multi-row selection (CollectionRowSelection) =====
   Ctrl/Shift-click a row's gutter to pick several, then drag them as one block.

   THE HIGHLIGHT IS AN OVERLAY CHILD, NOT THE ROW'S OWN BACKGROUND — and it has to be. ApplyRowSeparator
   writes background, borders, padding and margins INLINE (zebra tints, Card trays), and an inline style
   beats every rule in this file. A `.sasq-list-row--selected { background-color: … }` would therefore be
   invisible on exactly the rows most likely to be selected: the striped ones. The overlay is a sibling
   surface with nothing competing for it.

   Geometry (absolute, inset 0, 2px left rail, picking off) is set in C# beside the class, matching how
   every other row treatment splits paint from layout here. Reuses the existing accent tokens rather than
   minting new ones — a new token is a lockstep edit across BOTH theme sheets and the exported kit's baked
   twins, for a colour that already exists. */
.sasq-row-select-overlay {
    background-color: var(--sasq-accent-soft, rgba(46, 122, 217, 0.12));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
}

/* ===== List styles =====
   Two orthogonal axes: CollectionListStyle owns the CONTAINER (shell, gutter, density, ordinal), and
   CollectionRowSeparator — the .sasq-list-row--card rules above — owns the ROW SURFACE. Every style
   composes with every frame.

   THESE RULES MUST STAY BELOW .sasq-list-row / .sasq-list-row--card. They are single-class selectors just
   like those, so specificity TIES and source order is the only reason a style can drop the base row
   treatment. Note also what USS cannot reach here: ApplyRowSeparator writes background, borders, padding
   and margins INLINE, so a Card frame's tray fill and a zebra tint both beat every rule below — which is
   deliberate, an explicitly authored fill should win over a style's resting state. Anything that must
   override those (Minimal's air, Well's trough, removing a shell border) is applied in C# instead. */

/* --- Shared by every style ----------------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* Row actions (✕ ▲ ▼) fade in on row hover. The twin of the .sasq-table-row rule further up — a LIST row
   is not a .sasq-table-row, so without this the shared .sasq-table-row-action class would leave them at
   opacity 0 forever. Keep the two in lockstep. */
.sasq-list-row:hover .sasq-table-row-action {
    opacity: 1;
}

/* The ordinal lane. Stretched to the row's full height in C# so its edge (or Timeline's rail) is ONE
   unbroken vertical line — the strongest "orderly" cue available, and the reason a tall in-line-editor row
   still reads as part of the same column of rows. */
.sasq-list-gutter {
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

/* No brackets: "[3]" reads as debug output.
   `middle-*` is LOAD-BEARING, not cosmetic: MakeListGutter pins this label to the lane's top AND bottom, so
   the vertical half of the text-align is the only thing centring the number on the row. Change it to a
   `upper-*` variant and every ordinal jumps back to hugging the row's top edge. */
.sasq-list-ordinal {
    color: var(--sasq-text-dim, #7c7c7c);
    font-size: 10px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-right;
    transition-property: opacity;
    transition-duration: 0.12s;
}

/* The number IS the drag handle. Hover cross-fades the ordinal out and the grip in, occupying the SAME
   lane — so the handle costs no extra column, the lane never changes width, and nothing in the row
   reflows as the pointer travels down the list. The grip stays hit-testable while faded (opacity, not
   display), which is harmless: reaching it with the pointer is what reveals it.

   The fade-out is scoped to --draggable ON PURPOSE. A lane with no handle in it (a collection with reorder
   off, or ANY row while a sort/filter has reorder paused) has nothing to swap in, so an unscoped rule
   would simply make the number disappear under the pointer. */
.sasq-list-gutter-grip {
    opacity: 0;
    transition-property: opacity;
    transition-duration: 0.12s;
}
.sasq-list-row:hover .sasq-list-gutter-grip {
    opacity: 1;
}
.sasq-list-row:hover .sasq-list-gutter--draggable .sasq-list-ordinal {
    opacity: 0;
}

/* Count pill — deliberately the UnityEvent badge's exact recipe, so a count reads the same wherever it
   appears in the package. */
.sasq-list-count {
    color: var(--sasq-text-muted, #9a9a9a);
    font-size: 10px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    margin-left: 6px;
    padding: 0 6px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-08, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08));
    border-radius: 7px;
}

/* Header "+": a quiet icon, because the footer strip is the loud add affordance now. */
.sasq-list-add-header {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-width: 0;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}
.sasq-list-add-header:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-08, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08));
}

/* HOLD-TO-CLEAR, the leading button of the header group — deliberately the FURTHEST from the "+", because
   a destructive control next to the one people click most is a mis-click waiting to happen. Same quiet
   icon-button weight as its neighbours at rest; the commitment is shown by the progress ring the button
   paints over itself (CollectionClearAll.HoldRing), never by a colour the button wears while idle. The ring
   is an absolute overlay, so `overflow: visible` is what keeps it from being clipped to the padding box. */
.sasq-list-clear-header {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-width: 0;
    border-radius: 3px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    overflow: visible;
}
.sasq-list-clear-header:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-08, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08));
}

/* TRIAL: the list EYEDROPPER, sitting left of the header "+". Idle it is the same quiet icon button as its
   neighbour; ARMED it wears a soft accent fill and an accent border, so a mode that stays on until you turn
   it off is impossible to leave running without noticing. Not amber — amber means "this pointed somewhere
   and no longer does" in this package. */
.sasq-list-pick-header {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    /* The border is RESERVED, not absent: the button is content-sized (an 11px icon plus 4px of inline
       padding), so letting --armed introduce a 1px border grew the element by 2px on both axes and the
       header re-flowed on every arm/disarm. Transparent here, recoloured there. */
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-radius: 3px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}
.sasq-list-pick-header:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-08, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08));
}
.sasq-list-pick-header--armed {
    background-color: var(--sasq-accent-soft, rgba(46, 122, 217, 0.12));
    border-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
}
.sasq-list-pick-header--armed:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-accent-soft, rgba(46, 122, 217, 0.12));
}

/* Search + sort on ONE line. Three stacked full-width stock controls is what made the historical toolbar
   read like a debug panel rather than part of the inspector. */
.sasq-list-toolbar-line {
    margin-bottom: 4px;
}
.sasq-list-toolbar-line .sasq-collection-sortrow {
    margin-left: 6px;
}

/* Sort direction. Hidden outright unless a sort is active (C# owns `display`); when shown it is a SOFT
   accent button — a tinted fill and an accent border, so the control reads as something you can press and
   some of the accent is visible around the arrow rather than the glyph floating alone. It matches the
   "Sorted by X · reorder paused" note so the two read as ONE state. Not amber — amber means "this pointed
   somewhere and no longer does" in this package.
   Height comes from `align-self: stretch` in C#, which matches the sort dropdown beside it. */
.sasq-list-sortdir {
    background-color: var(--sasq-accent-soft, rgba(46, 122, 217, 0.12));
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 0 7px;
    margin-left: 3px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}
.sasq-list-sortdir:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-accent-softer, rgba(46, 122, 217, 0.24));
}

/* The sort note's direction arrow — a real icon rather than a "▲" text glyph. */
.sasq-sortnote-dir {
    margin-left: 3px;
    margin-right: 3px;
}

/* Footer add strip. Outlined rather than filled so it reads as "there is room for more here" instead of
   competing with the rows above it.
   NOT full width, and that is a functional constraint rather than a taste one: EditorSpringFX.ButtonSpring
   SCALES the button on hover, so an edge-to-edge strip grew past the collection's content box and got
   clipped — you could not see the whole thing at the moment you were pointing at it. Shrink-wrapped to its
   own content plus generous padding, centred, it has room to grow into. */
.sasq-list-add-footer {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    align-self: center;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin: 6px 0 2px 0;
    padding: 3px 22px;
}
.sasq-list-add-footer:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-05, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05));
    border-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
}
.sasq-list-add-footer-label {
    color: var(--sasq-text-muted, #9a9a9a);
    font-size: 11px;
    margin-left: 5px;
}

/* Empty state as a designed panel, not a loose sentence. */
.sasq-list-empty {
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-03, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03));
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--sasq-ink-08, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08));
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 10px 8px;
    margin: 2px 0 4px 0;
}

/* --- Style: Rows (default) ----------------------------------------------------------------------- */
/* A bordered shell with a crisp gutter edge. No fill on the row itself at rest — the frame and the gutter
   edge carry the structure, and a permanent wash on every row is most of what made the historical list
   look striped-by-default. */
.sasq-list-row--rows {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
}
.sasq-list-row--rows:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-04, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04));
}
.sasq-list-row--rows .sasq-list-gutter {
    border-right-width: 1px;
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-row-divider, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1));
    margin-right: 8px;
}
.sasq-list-row--rows .sasq-list-ordinal {
    padding-right: 6px;
}

/* --- Style: Minimal ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
/* Premium via restraint: no shell (removed in C#), no row fill, and air instead of lines. The gutter edge
   is fainter than Rows' — it is the only structural line left, so it should whisper. */
.sasq-list-row--minimal {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
}
.sasq-list-row--minimal:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-05, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05));
}
.sasq-list-row--minimal .sasq-list-gutter {
    border-right-width: 1px;
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-ink-08, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08));
    margin-right: 10px;
}
.sasq-list-row--minimal .sasq-list-ordinal {
    padding-right: 7px;
}
/* The header carries the structure once the box is gone, so it takes the weight the box used to have. */
.sasq-list--minimal .sasq-collection-header {
    font-size: 12px;
}

/* --- Style: Timeline ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
/* A continuous rail down the list with each ordinal as a node on it, over a RECESSED WELL (fill + top edge
   set in C#). A list IS an ordered thing; this is the style that says so. The well is not decoration: with
   a transparent body this was a rail floating on nothing and read as a variant of Minimal — the darker
   surface is what gives the rail and its nodes something to sit on, and it is why a separate "Well" style
   turned out to be unnecessary.
   The rail is one absolutely-positioned element behind the rows (AttachTimelineRail), capped to the first
   and last node — a rail running past the last row reads as "there's more below", the same reason the last
   row never gets a hairline. No gutter border here: the rail IS the edge. */
.sasq-list-rail {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-14, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14));
}
.sasq-list-row--timeline {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
}
.sasq-list-row--timeline:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-05, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05));
}
.sasq-list-row--timeline .sasq-list-gutter {
    margin-right: 6px;
}
/* The node disc the ordinal sits in, and that the rail threads through. Filled with the WELL colour rather
   than left transparent, so the rail is hidden behind the disc instead of striking through the number. */
.sasq-list-node {
    background-color: var(--sasq-well-bg, #1e1e1e);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
    border-radius: 8px;
    transition-property: background-color, border-color;
    transition-duration: 0.12s;
}
.sasq-list-row--timeline .sasq-list-ordinal {
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}
/* Hovering lights the node, so the thing you are about to grab is the thing that responds. */
.sasq-list-row--timeline:hover .sasq-list-node {
    background-color: var(--sasq-accent-soft, rgba(46, 122, 217, 0.12));
    border-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
}

/* 3-line reorder handle. The lines are a single GripGlyph (device-pixel-snapped Painter2D)
   rather than stacked 1px elements, which round to uneven heights at fractional display
   scaling; its rest/hover colors are set in code (MakeReorderGrip). */
.sasq-reorder-grip {
    width: 14px;
    height: 7px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    margin-left: 2px;
    margin-right: 4px;
    align-self: center;
}

/* Prevent list/foldout chevrons from being clipped inside collapsible group contents */
.sasq-group-content .unity-foldout {
    margin-left: 15px;
    margin-right: 4px;
}

/* ===== Color Palette widget (inspector) ===== */
/* The swatch SLOT — the stable hit target (cursor + click live here). It never moves, so the animated
   visual inside can rise/scale without sliding out from under the cursor. */
.sasq-swatch {
    cursor: link;
    position: relative;
}
.sasq-swatch--grid {
    margin: 0;
}
/* One explicit NoWrap line of the grid. The grid is a COLUMN of these and never uses flex-wrap: a wrapping
   row's height is measured by the parent through a different width than it lays out at, so the field draws a
   swatch line outside its own box and overlaps the field above. See BindingFactory.ColorPalette. */
.sasq-swatch-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: nowrap;
}
.sasq-swatch--bar {
    margin: 0;
}
/* The animated colored block (this is what the spring scales/translates). Fills the slot.
   Its border sits OVER the swatch color — skin-neutral.

   THE RIM COLOUR BELOW IS A FALLBACK ONLY. BindingFactory.SwatchRimColor writes it inline, per swatch,
   because the right rim depends on how dark the swatch is: a fixed 16% white over a NEAR-BLACK fill
   composites onto the editor's own panel grey, so the rim reads as background and the swatch looks a
   pixel narrower each side than its light neighbours. The `:hover` rule below is likewise superseded
   inline (an inline border colour beats USS), and is driven from the same pointer callbacks. */
.sasq-swatch-visual {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--sasq-swatch-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16));
}
.sasq-swatch-visual--grid {
    border-radius: 4px;
}
.sasq-swatch:hover .sasq-swatch-visual {
    border-color: var(--sasq-swatch-border-hover, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6));
}
/* Inset selection ring (color set inline, adaptive). Inset so neighbours never clip it. */
.sasq-swatch-ring {
    position: absolute;
    left: 2px;
    top: 2px;
    right: 2px;
    bottom: 2px;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-radius: 3px;
}
/* "+" tile that appends the field's current color to the palette. The tile itself is a bare grid CELL; the
   drawn box is the child below, inset by the swatch gap exactly like .sasq-swatch-visual is — so the tile
   fills one column instead of one column plus a margin. */
.sasq-swatch--add {
    margin: 0;
}
.sasq-swatch--add-fill {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-04, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04));
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
    border-radius: 4px;
}
.sasq-swatch--add:hover .sasq-swatch--add-fill {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-10, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1));
}
/* Absolute-fill + middle-center guarantees the glyph is centered regardless of the tile's flex setup. */
.sasq-swatch-add-glyph {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    color: var(--sasq-add-glyph, #b0b0b0);
    font-size: 15px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}
/* The optional current-color bar (a standard ColorField).
   The HORIZONTAL zeroes matter as much as the vertical ones. The bar lives inside the widget's own input
   column, where the .sasq-binding-row right-edge normalizer (direct children only) cannot reach it, so it
   keeps the editor theme's inspector-field margins — 3px on the left and MINUS 2px on the right, meant for a
   field that spans a whole inspector row. Inside a fixed-width bar+gear lane those are just noise that the
   lane's minWidth reservation in BindingFactory.ColorPalette (kColorBarMinWidth + kGearLaneWidth) cannot
   account for: leave them in and the gear ends up 1px outside the lane it was reserved room in. */
.sasq-swatch-colorbar {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 0;
}
/* Transient "Copied #hex" toast that springs in over the field. */
.sasq-swatch-toast {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    background-color: var(--sasq-popup-bg-heavy, rgba(20, 20, 20, 0.92));
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-popup-heavy-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18));
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-popup-heavy-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18));
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-popup-heavy-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-popup-heavy-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18));
    border-width: 1px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 2px 7px;
    color: var(--sasq-toast-text, #d7f0d7);
    font-size: 10px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
}
/* "No palette assigned" prompt shown inside an unconfigured ColorPalette field. */
.sasq-swatch-empty {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-03, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03));
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-width: 1px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 8px 10px;
}
.sasq-swatch-empty-msg {
    color: var(--sasq-empty-msg, #aeaeae);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    white-space: normal;
}
.sasq-swatch-empty-btn {
    flex-grow: 1;
    margin-right: 4px;
}
/* Gear at the right edge of the color bar — picks the palette / opens the palette window. */
.sasq-swatch-gear {
    width: 20px;
    height: 18px;
    margin-left: 3px;
    margin-right: 0;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding: 0;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-width: 0;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}
.sasq-swatch-gear:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-08, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08));
    border-radius: 3px;
}

/* ===== Rich Text editor widget ===== */
.sasq-richtext-input .unity-base-text-field__input {
    border-top-left-radius: 4px;
    border-top-right-radius: 4px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;
}
/* The nested raw TextField lives in the wrapper's input column, where the .sasq-binding-row right-edge
   normalizer (it only reaches direct children / property-field children) can't touch it — so it keeps the
   editor theme's default horizontal field margin and its right border/rounding gets clipped (the left looks
   rounded + outlined, the right does not). Zero its horizontal margins so it sits flush and the dark rounded
   outline shows symmetrically on both sides. */
.sasq-richtext-field .sasq-richtext-input {
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 0;
}
/* The formatting toolbar (a column: button bar on top, an expandable chip row below). */
.sasq-richtext-toolbar {
    margin-bottom: 3px;
}
.sasq-richtext-bar {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
}
/* B / I / U / Color / Size buttons — compact, flat, non-focusable. */
.sasq-richtext-btn {
    min-width: 22px;
    height: 18px;
    padding: 0 6px;
    margin: 0 3px 0 0;
    font-size: 11px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-05, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05));
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-radius: 3px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}
.sasq-richtext-btn:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
}
/* Active (its chip row is open). */
.sasq-richtext-btn--on {
    background-color: var(--sasq-richtext-on-bg, rgba(90, 140, 220, 0.35));
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-richtext-on-border, rgba(120, 170, 240, 0.7));
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-richtext-on-border, rgba(120, 170, 240, 0.7));
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-richtext-on-border, rgba(120, 170, 240, 0.7));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-richtext-on-border, rgba(120, 170, 240, 0.7));
}
/* Expandable Color / Size chip row under the bar. */
.sasq-richtext-chiprow {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 3px;
}
/* A palette color chip (click wraps the selection in <color=#hex>). Border sits over the chip color —
   skin-neutral. */
.sasq-richtext-swatch {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    margin: 2px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18);
    cursor: link;
}
.sasq-richtext-swatch:hover {
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75);
    scale: 1.12 1.12;
}
/* A Size / More tag chip (click wraps the selection in the matching tag). */
.sasq-richtext-tagchip {
    height: 18px;
    padding: 0 7px;
    margin: 2px;
    font-size: 11px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-05, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05));
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-radius: 3px;
}
.sasq-richtext-tagchip:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-12, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-ink-28, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28));
}
/* The free ColorField in the Color row — compact, sits inline with the swatch chips. */
.sasq-richtext-colorfield {
    width: 46px;
    min-width: 46px;
    height: 18px;
    margin: 2px 4px 2px 2px;
}
.sasq-richtext-colorfield .unity-base-field__input {
    min-height: 16px;
    margin: 0;
}
/* The palette gear in the Color row (an icon-only .sasq-richtext-btn). */
.sasq-richtext-gear {
    padding: 0 4px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}
/* Blue "drop here" outline shown at the slot a dragged gradient preset will land in (accent
   affordance — skin-neutral). */
.sasq-gradient-drop-indicator {
    border-width: 2px;
    border-color: rgba(80, 150, 240, 0.95);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background-color: rgba(80, 150, 240, 0.12);
}

/* Custom selection highlight overlay for the rich-text field (shown when the native one is gone — e.g. while
   the color picker window holds focus — so you always see which text you're coloring). */
.sasq-richtext-selhl {
    background-color: rgba(80, 140, 220, 0.45);
    border-radius: 2px;
}

/* The "Clear" chip in the Color row (only shown when the selection already has a color). Red washes —
   skin-neutral. */
.sasq-richtext-clearchip {
    background-color: rgba(220, 90, 90, 0.18);
    border-color: rgba(220, 90, 90, 0.55);
}
.sasq-richtext-clearchip:hover {
    background-color: rgba(220, 90, 90, 0.30);
    border-color: rgba(235, 110, 110, 0.85);
}
/* Tiny dim caption above the preview bubble. */
.sasq-richtext-caption {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-caption, #7d7d7d);
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    margin-top: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
}
/* The live formatted preview "result bubble" (background color is applied inline from the node option). */
.sasq-richtext-preview {
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-ink-14, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14));
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-ink-14, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14));
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-ink-14, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-ink-14, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14));
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 7px 9px;
    min-height: 22px;
}
.sasq-richtext-preview-label {
    white-space: normal;
    color: var(--sasq-text-preview, #e4e4e4);
    font-size: 12px;
}
/* Minimizable preview header — chevron + dim "PREVIEW" label, click to spring the preview open/closed. */
.sasq-richtext-preview-header {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
    padding-top: 1px;
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    cursor: link;
}
.sasq-richtext-preview-header:hover .sasq-richtext-caption {
    color: var(--sasq-text-caption-hover, #c0c0c0);
}

/* ===== Color Palette window ===== */
.sasq-palettewin-title {
    font-size: 15px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    color: var(--sasq-text-title, #d6d6d6);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
}
.sasq-palettewin-hint {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-muted, #9a9a9a);
    margin-bottom: 2px;
    white-space: normal;
}
.sasq-palettewin-status {
    font-size: 11px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    color: var(--sasq-success-text, #7fd28b);
    min-height: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
}
/* A browse swatch: big rounded block above its hex (and optional name). Block border sits over the
   swatch color — skin-neutral. */
.sasq-palettewin-card {
    align-items: center;
    width: 64px;
    margin: 4px;
}
.sasq-palettewin-block {
    width: 56px;
    height: 40px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16);
    cursor: link;
}
.sasq-palettewin-card:hover .sasq-palettewin-block {
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
}
.sasq-palettewin-hex {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-label, #c8c8c8);
    margin-top: 2px;
}
.sasq-palettewin-name {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-soft, #8a8a8a);
}

/* ===== Custom UnityEvent drawer ===== */
.sasq-uevent {
    margin-top: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
}
.sasq-uevent-header {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    background-color: var(--sasq-header-bg, #383838);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-left-radius: 4px;
    border-top-right-radius: 4px;
    padding: 3px 6px;
    cursor: link;
}
.sasq-uevent-header:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-header-bg-hover, #424242);
}
.sasq-uevent-chevron {
    color: var(--sasq-text-muted, #9a9a9a);
    font-size: 10px;
    width: 12px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}
.sasq-uevent-title {
    color: var(--sasq-text-title, #d6d6d6);
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    margin-left: 2px;
}
.sasq-uevent-typehint {
    color: var(--sasq-text-dim, #7c7c7c);
    font-size: 10px;
    margin-left: 4px;
}
.sasq-uevent-badge {
    color: var(--sasq-banner-fg, #c9d6e8);
    font-size: 10px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    margin-left: 6px;
    padding: 0 6px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-08, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08));
    border-radius: 7px;
}
.sasq-uevent-body {
    background-color: var(--sasq-group-content-bg, #2b2b2b);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-width: 0 1px 1px 1px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;
    padding: 6px;
}
.sasq-uevent-empty {
    color: var(--sasq-text-dim, #7c7c7c);
    -unity-font-style: italic;
    padding: 4px 2px;
}
.sasq-uevent-card {
    background-color: var(--sasq-card-bg, #313131);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
    border-width: 1px 1px 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 5px 6px;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
    transition-property: border-left-color;
    transition-duration: 0.15s;
}
/* Left-edge color bar = call state at a glance (only border-left-color is overridden). The three state
   colors are status hues — skin-neutral. */
.sasq-uevent-card--state-off {
    border-left-color: #6e6e6e;
}
.sasq-uevent-card--state-editor-runtime {
    border-left-color: #10b981;
}
.sasq-uevent-card--state-runtime-only {
    border-left-color: #3b82f6;
}
/* A listener with no function on it gives up its status stripe ENTIRELY — a call state on something that can
   never run is a status light on a dead wire. Stripe present = this listener does something; that binary is
   what you read peripherally, with no colour vocabulary to learn and nothing lost to colour blindness. Must
   stay AFTER the three state rules: same specificity, so source order is what makes it win. Only the border
   is touched, never the fill — UnityEventCardColor writes the background INLINE, which beats any stylesheet. */
.sasq-uevent-card--unwired {
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border-strong, #1e1e1e);
}
/* Optional density tweak from the designer's Compact toggle (the layout is always 2-row). */
.sasq-uevent-card--compact {
    padding: 3px 5px;
    margin-bottom: 3px;
}
.sasq-uevent-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 3px;
}
/* The function button is a MENU, not a text field. It sat at the same fill, border and height as the target
   ObjectField directly above it, so the card read as two identical slabs with nothing saying "this opens
   something". Recessed a step, and it carries a caret at its right edge. Its content is built as child
   labels (not the Button's own text) so the method name can out-weigh its breadcrumb prefix. */
.sasq-uevent-method {
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    -unity-text-align: middle-left;
    background-color: var(--sasq-well-bg, #1e1e1e);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
}
.sasq-uevent-method:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-control-bg-hover, #353535);
}
/* Breadcrumb prefix ("Event Picker Audio #2 ▸") — only present when it says something the ObjectField above
   doesn't, and dimmed when it is, so the method name is what the eye lands on. */
.sasq-uevent-method-prefix {
    -unity-font-style: normal;
    color: var(--sasq-text-muted, #9a9a9a);
    flex-shrink: 1;
    overflow: hidden;
}
.sasq-uevent-method-name {
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    color: var(--sasq-text-title, #d6d6d6);
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-shrink: 1;
    overflow: hidden;
}
/* The empty state ("Select a function…") in the voice .sasq-uevent-empty already uses for an absence. It was
   previously drawn bold at --sasq-text-title, i.e. the loudest text the card has, so at a glance an unassigned
   listener weighed exactly as much as a real one. AFTER .sasq-uevent-method-name — equal specificity, so source
   order decides. Amber is not reused here: that means "this pointed somewhere and no longer does". */
.sasq-uevent-method-name--empty {
    -unity-font-style: italic;
    color: var(--sasq-text-dim, #7c7c7c);
}
.sasq-uevent-method-caret {
    color: var(--sasq-text-muted, #9a9a9a);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-left: 4px;
    font-size: 9px;
}
.sasq-uevent-iconbtn {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-width: 0;
}
.sasq-uevent-iconbtn:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-08, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08));
}
/* The clear-function button is only occasionally relevant, so it stays out of the way until you are actually
   working on this listener — the same opacity reveal the Script Header's buttons use. It remains hit-testable
   while faded, which is harmless: reaching it with the pointer is what reveals it. It lives INSIDE the method
   well (see UnityEventWidget), so this stays a descendant rule off the card. */
.sasq-uevent-clear {
    opacity: 0;
    transition-property: opacity;
    transition-duration: 0.12s;
}
.sasq-uevent-card:hover .sasq-uevent-clear {
    opacity: 1;
}
/* The "dynamic" tag that stands in for the static-argument field when the event supplies the value itself.
   It sits in the arg column so that column always answers one question — a box you type in, or the event.
   NO color here on purpose: it is set inline from WidgetPalette.AccentIcon, the same token the method
   picker's dynamic column uses, because the tag only teaches anything if it is that exact blue and a
   second declaration here would be free to drift from it. Bold for the same reason the picker is. */
.sasq-uevent-dynamic {
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    font-size: 10px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-left: 2px;
    align-self: center;
}

/* ===== Animation Curve editor widget ===== */
/* Root marker (also the verification-test hook). The Painter2D surface paints all curve visuals;
   USS only styles the surrounding chrome — one consistent button/field language for all rows. */
.sasq-animation-curve-field {
}
.sasq-curve-label {
    margin-bottom: 2px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-label, #c8c8c8);
}
.sasq-curve-well {
    background-color: var(--sasq-well-bg, #1e1e1e);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
}
.sasq-curve-preview {
    margin-left: 6px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}
.sasq-curve-surface {
}

/* The single, consistent button style shared by presets, Frame, Edit, and the tangent-mode toggles (#1). */
.sasq-curve-ribbon {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 4px;
}
.sasq-curve-btn {
    height: 18px;
    min-height: 18px;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: var(--sasq-control-bg, #2b2b2b);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-body, #cfcfcf);
    font-size: 11px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 7px;
    padding-right: 7px;
    margin-top: 1px;
    margin-bottom: 1px;
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 3px;
}
.sasq-curve-btn:hover {
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    color: var(--sasq-text-strong, #ffffff);
}
.sasq-curve-btn--active {
    background-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    color: #ffffff;
}

/* Two stacked action rows so the selected-key controls never overflow at default inspector width:
   row 1 = tangent shaping, row 2 = Time/Value (left) + Frame/Edit (right). */
.sasq-curve-actionrow {
    flex-direction: column;
    margin-top: 4px;
}
.sasq-curve-tangentrow {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.sasq-curve-fieldsrow {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 3px;
}
.sasq-curve-keyfields {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
}
/* Vertical separator that sets the Both/One handle toggle apart from the tangent-shape buttons (#3). */
.sasq-curve-divider {
    width: 1px;
    height: 14px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-divider, #4a4a4a);
    margin-left: 4px;
    margin-right: 6px;
}
/* The handle-mode toggle reads as its own control (a touch wider + a faint outline even when inactive). */
.sasq-curve-handlebtn {
    min-width: 40px;
}
.sasq-curve-cap {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-muted, #9a9a9a);
    margin-right: 4px;
    align-self: center;
}
.sasq-curve-numrow {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    margin-left: 4px;
}
.sasq-curve-num {
    width: 44px;
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 0;
}
.sasq-curve-num .unity-base-field__input {
    min-height: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    font-size: 11px;
}
.sasq-curve-fold-content {
    margin-top: 4px;
}

/* Axis numbers + editable Max fields (overlay children; #6, #10). */
.sasq-curve-axis-label {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-axis, rgba(195, 195, 195, 0.55));
}
.sasq-curve-maxfield {
    width: 48px;
}
.sasq-curve-maxfield .unity-base-field__input {
    height: 15px;
    min-height: 15px;
    font-size: 10px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-well-bg-soft, rgba(30, 30, 30, 0.85));
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
}

/* Resizable well drag handle (#7). */
.sasq-curve-resize-handle {
    height: 9px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    cursor: resize-vertical;
}
.sasq-curve-resize-handle:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-05, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05));
    border-radius: 0 0 4px 4px;
}

/* Window: collapsible "Controls" info box + preset swatch gallery (#9, #10). */
.sasq-curve-controls-box {
    margin-top: 4px;
    padding-top: 4px;
    padding-bottom: 4px;
    padding-left: 6px;
    padding-right: 6px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-box-bg, #232323);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-radius: 4px;
}
.sasq-curve-controls-header {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    cursor: link;
}
.sasq-curve-controls-fold {
    margin-top: 4px;
}
.sasq-curve-swatch-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
}
.sasq-curve-swatch {
    width: 38px;
    height: 24px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-well-bg, #1e1e1e);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-radius: 3px;
    margin-right: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    cursor: link;
}
.sasq-curve-swatch:hover {
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    background-color: var(--sasq-swatch-hover-bg, #242424);
}
.sasq-curve-swatch-add {
    background-color: var(--sasq-control-bg, #2b2b2b);
}
.sasq-curve-swatch-plus {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-muted, #9a9a9a);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}
.sasq-curve-swatch-add:hover .sasq-curve-swatch-plus {
    color: var(--sasq-text-strong, #ffffff);
}
/* Icon-only buttons (Frame / Edit / preset ⋮): square, snug, same 18px height as the rest. */
.sasq-curve-iconbtn {
    width: 22px;
    min-width: 22px;
    padding-left: 2px;
    padding-right: 2px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}
/* Wrap-mode dropdowns (full editor). */
.sasq-curve-wrap-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
}
.sasq-curve-wrap-field {
    margin-right: 10px;
    min-width: 150px;
}
.sasq-curve-hint {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-hint, rgba(200, 200, 200, 0.45));
    margin-top: 4px;
    white-space: normal;
}


/* ===== Gradient editor widget ===== */
.sasq-gradient-field {
}
.sasq-gradient-label {
    margin-bottom: 2px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-label, #c8c8c8);
}
/* The strip well — rounded + inset dark border + overflow hidden (mirrors .sasq-curve-well). */
.sasq-gradient-well {
    background-color: var(--sasq-well-bg, #1e1e1e);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
}
.sasq-gradient-preview {
    margin-left: 6px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}
/* The pin surface fills the well; the composited strip is set as its background image by the control. */
.sasq-gradient-surface {
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
}
/* Preset ribbon swatches show a mini gradient via background-image — stretch it to fill the swatch box. */
.sasq-gradient-preset-swatch {
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
}

/* Resizable strip drag handle (mirrors .sasq-curve-resize-handle). */
.sasq-gradient-resize-handle {
    height: 9px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    cursor: resize-vertical;
}
.sasq-gradient-resize-handle:hover {
    background-color: var(--sasq-ink-05, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05));
    border-radius: 0 0 4px 4px;
}

/* Action row + blend-mode segmented control (reuses the curve button language). */
.sasq-gradient-actionrow {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 4px;
}
.sasq-gradient-seg {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
}
.sasq-gradient-seg-btn {
    height: 18px;
    min-height: 18px;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: var(--sasq-control-bg, #2b2b2b);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    color: var(--sasq-text-body, #cfcfcf);
    font-size: 11px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 7px;
    padding-right: 7px;
    margin-top: 1px;
    margin-bottom: 1px;
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 0;
}
.sasq-gradient-seg-btn:hover {
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    color: var(--sasq-text-strong, #ffffff);
}
.sasq-gradient-seg-btn--active {
    background-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    color: #ffffff;
}
.sasq-gradient-seg-btn--first {
    border-radius: 3px 0 0 3px;
}
.sasq-gradient-seg-btn--last {
    border-radius: 0 3px 3px 0;
}

/* ===== Enum Badge Grid widget =====
   A grid of clickable toggle chips replacing the enum dropdown. Active / partial colors are applied INLINE
   from the node's resolved accent (per-node) — USS only carries shape, text and the non-accent states. */
.sasq-enum-badge-field .unity-base-field__label {
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-top: 3px;
}
.sasq-enum-badge-grid {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
}
/* Fixed-column grid cell: takes exactly 1/cols of the row; its padding is the inter-badge gap. */
.sasq-enum-badge-cell {
    flex-direction: row;
    padding-right: 4px;
    padding-bottom: 4px;
}
.sasq-enum-badge {
    height: 20px;
    min-height: 20px;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: var(--sasq-control-bg, #2b2b2b);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-body, #cfcfcf);
    font-size: 11px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 8px;
    padding-right: 8px;
    margin-top: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 4px;
    /* A CHIP THAT CANNOT FIT ITS NAME MUST TRUNCATE, NOT SPILL. In fixed-column mode the cells are an
       exact 1/cols share of the row, so a narrow host hands each chip a width its label may not fit —
       measured in a 90px split pane at "Columns: 3": 30px cells, a 26px button, and "Single" wanting
       ~49px. Centred text with no clip then overflows BOTH sides equally and the pane's own clip cut the
       left off, so the chip rendered as "ingle": it reads as a rendering fault rather than as a chip that
       is too small. Ellipsis keeps the overflow inside the chip and says what is actually true. Costs
       nothing whenever the label fits, which is every roomy layout.

       THE 8px SIDE PADDING BELOW IS NEGOTIABLE, and SasquatchEnumBadgeControl.KeepOneGlyphVisible writes
       over it INLINE on a chip whose width is dictated from outside. Truncation has a last step that reads
       as a rendering fault of its own: under "one letter + the ellipsis" Unity draws the ellipsis ALONE, so
       a squeezed chip renders as "…". The chip therefore trades this padding away — down to a 1px floor,
       and only as far as the fit demands — before it gives up the word. Change the 8 here and change
       BadgePadX there (and EnumChipPadX in ExportedWidgetKit) in the same pass; the fit holds them as
       constants precisely so it never reads back its own last answer. */
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
}
.sasq-enum-badge:hover {
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    color: var(--sasq-text-strong, #ffffff);
}
.sasq-enum-badge--active {
    /* background-color, border-color AND color are set inline from the resolved accent — the ink is picked
       for contrast against that badge's own fill (SasquatchEnumBadgeControl.Refresh), because a flat white
       label disappears on a light tint. This white is only the pre-inline fallback; it never paints on a
       built badge, and the inline value also beats the :hover rule above. */
    color: #ffffff;
    /* Non-color selection cue: a thicker bottom border reads as "selected" even in grayscale / for colorblind
       users, not only via the accent fill. The badge has a fixed 20px height, so the extra border grows inward —
       no layout jitter, no width change. */
    border-bottom-width: 3px;
}
.sasq-enum-badge--mixed {
    color: var(--sasq-mixed-fg, #9e9e9e);
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-mixed-border, #6a6a6a);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-mixed-border, #6a6a6a);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-mixed-border, #6a6a6a);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-mixed-border, #6a6a6a);
}
.sasq-enum-badge--special {
    -unity-font-style: italic;
}

/* Optional Text Backdrop (accessibility), the twin of .sasq-button__backdrop and
   .sasq-progress-label-backdrop: a hugging dark pill inside the chip's centering row, carrying the label AND
   any per-value icon so neither can be lost against a bright accent or a light per-value tint.

   The pill's PAINT is a separate --lit class rather than part of this rule, because a badge is the one of the
   three whose fill is only user-colored HALF the time: an idle chip is the theme's own control background under
   the theme's own body ink, already readable by construction, and a permanent dark pill on it would read as a
   box inside a box (and, in the light skin, as a black smear). The pill's SPACE is reserved in both states —
   transparent border included — so lighting a badge never changes its width and the grid never re-flows. */
.sasq-enum-badge__row {
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}
.sasq-enum-badge__backdrop {
    max-width: 100%;
    flex-shrink: 1;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-right-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-bottom-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-left-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 6px;
    padding-right: 6px;
}
.sasq-enum-badge__backdrop--lit {
    background-color: rgba(10, 10, 10, 0.62);
    border-top-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    border-right-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    border-bottom-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    border-left-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
}

/* Mixed (multi-object) value state for text readouts (dropdowns, min/max labels, scene).
   Graphical widgets (progress/gradient/curve/color/spring/toggle) mute inline from WidgetPalette.Mixed. */
.sasq-mixed-text {
    -unity-font-style: italic;
    color: var(--sasq-mixed-fg, #9e9e9e);
}

/* Palette swatch row under the editor. */
.sasq-gradient-swatch-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
}
.sasq-gradient-swatch {
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-radius: 3px;
    margin-right: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    cursor: link;
}
.sasq-gradient-swatch:hover {
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
}

/* Glassmorphic live drag tooltip — same recipe as .sasq-swatch-toast. */
.sasq-gradient-tip {
    position: absolute;
    background-color: var(--sasq-popup-bg-heavy, rgba(20, 20, 20, 0.92));
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-popup-heavy-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18));
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-popup-heavy-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18));
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-popup-heavy-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18));
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-popup-heavy-border, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18));
    border-width: 1px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding-top: 1px;
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    padding-left: 6px;
    padding-right: 6px;
    color: var(--sasq-tip-text, #eaeaea);
    font-size: 10px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
}

/* Window: controls box + pin-layout row + hint (mirror the curve classes). */
.sasq-gradient-controls-box {
    margin-top: 4px;
    padding-top: 4px;
    padding-bottom: 4px;
    padding-left: 6px;
    padding-right: 6px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-box-bg, #232323);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-radius: 4px;
}
.sasq-gradient-wrap-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
}
.sasq-gradient-hint {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--sasq-text-hint, rgba(200, 200, 200, 0.45));
    margin-top: 4px;
    white-space: normal;
}

/* Color popover (anchored to a clicked color pin). */
.sasq-gradient-popover-grid {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.sasq-gradient-popover-swatch {
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    border-radius: 3px;
    margin-right: 3px;
    margin-bottom: 3px;
    cursor: link;
}
.sasq-gradient-popover-swatch:hover {
    border-top-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-right-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-bottom-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
}

/* While the format painter is armed the canvas root carries .sasq-painting, which USS can hang
   paint-mode styling off. The CURSOR is deliberately NOT here: the armed cursor is a rasterized
   paint-roller texture (SasquatchIcons.RenderCursorTexture), and USS `cursor` can only name a
   built-in keyword or a project asset — neither of which a generated texture is. It is written
   inline per node surface instead (SyncPainterSurfaces), which also beats any rule placed here,
   so re-adding a `cursor:` declaration below would be dead style. */

/* ==== Button presets ====
   Structural styling only — the accent-derived colors, radius, and hover feedback are inline
   (per-node dynamic values; inline always beats USS pseudo-states). Classic buttons carry NONE
   of these classes: they are Unity's stock button, untouched. */
.sasq-button {
    padding-left: 12px;
    padding-right: 12px;
}
.sasq-button__row {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-grow: 1;
}
.sasq-button__icon {
    margin-right: 6px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}
.sasq-button__icon--right {
    margin-right: 0;
    margin-left: 6px;
}

/* Text Backdrop: a hugging dark pill inside the centering row, holding the label AND the icon so
   neither can be lost against a bright accent. Mirrors .sasq-progress-label-backdrop; the row keeps
   the centering, so the pill only ever needs to lay out its own content. */
.sasq-button__backdrop {
    max-width: 100%;
    flex-shrink: 1;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: rgba(10, 10, 10, 0.62);
    border-radius: 8px;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    padding: 1px 7px;
}
/* Label riding the pill: always light-on-dark, whatever the preset's own ink is. */
.sasq-button__label--boxed {
    color: #ffffff;
}



/* ==== Inspector field search ====
   Rows/containers whose text matched the filter carry an accent left stripe (a filter, not a
   highlight — per-glyph highlighting can't be injected uniformly across the widget label paths).
   Inline border-left values (section tint / accent stripe rails) win over this class by design,
   so already-railed cards keep their own color. Fallback equals the dark-token value. */
.sasq-search-match {
    border-left-width: 2px;
    border-left-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
}


/* ==== Prefab-override bar on a custom-drawn widget ====
   Unity paints the bar from inside its own two-way binding, so it only ever appears on a widget that went
   through BindProperty. Everything hand-drawn (Enum Badge Grid, Progress Bar, Rating, Gradient, Tag Chips…)
   showed NOTHING for a genuinely overridden value. BindingFactory.ArmPrefabOverrideBar adds this class only
   when Unity is not already marking the field, so a natively bound row keeps exactly one bar — Unity's.

   Matches the editor theme's own override rail: a solid 2px bar hard against the field's left edge, using
   the margin trick so the bar sits OUTSIDE the field's content box and cannot reflow the row. Deliberately
   NOT keyed to Unity's `unity-binding--prefab-override` name, which is theirs to rename on a version hop. */
.sasq-prefab-override {
    border-left-width: 2px;
    border-left-color: rgb(31, 122, 255);
    margin-left: -2px;
    padding-left: 0;
}


/* ==== Live Debug rows ====
   The graph strip a field grows under itself while Live Debug is recording. Deliberately its OWN row rather
   than a sparkline beside the field: the field row stays untouched, so no widget is squeezed and a Vector3
   cannot push the inspector into horizontal scroll (the help chip hit exactly that). It also leaves room for
   the readout and the min/max pins, which a beside-the-field trace has nowhere to put.

   Colours are set inline from WidgetPalette at construction (the paint callback runs outside the build's
   palette scope), so these rules own only geometry plus the two surfaces that never vary. Fallbacks equal
   the dark-token values, matching every other rule in this file. */
.sasq-debug-wrapper {
    flex-direction: column;
}

.sasq-debug-row {
    margin-top: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
}

.sasq-debug-well {
    border-radius: 3px;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
    background-color: var(--sasq-well-bg, #1e1e1e);
}

/* Reuses the audio waveform's playhead colour: one "you are looking at this instant" tell across the package. */
.sasq-debug-playhead {
    background-color: var(--sasq-playhead, #e0b020);
}

.sasq-debug-ghost {
    -unity-font-style: italic;
}

.sasq-debug-readout {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
}

/* The moment card floats over the built tree, so it needs to sit above every row it may overlap. */
.sasq-debug-card {
    position: absolute;
}

/* The code peek is a SEPARATE card beside the moment card, never a pane inside it — growing and shrinking the
   card someone is reading, while the row they are aiming at moves, is not something eyes can follow. */
.sasq-debug-peek {
    position: absolute;
}

/* The playhead transport — one per inspector, directly under the Script Header. Hidden until recording arms.
   Fallbacks equal the dark-token values (pixel armor), same contract as every other rule in this file.

   Every button here is a square icon button of ONE size. The first version mixed unicode glyphs with text
   labels ("Clear", "CSV"), so each control was whatever width its own characters happened to be and the row
   read as a jumble rather than as a toolbar. Uniform geometry is what makes a strip of controls scan. */
.sasq-debug-transport {
    border-radius: 3px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-control-bg, #2b2b2b);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
}

/* Pinned state — the bar has floated free of the flow to stay reachable in a long inspector. It needs to look
   like it is ABOVE the content, or a toolbar sitting on top of a field reads as a rendering bug. */
.sasq-debug-transport--pinned {
    border-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
    background-color: var(--sasq-control-bg, #2b2b2b);
}

.sasq-debug-transport__btn {
    width: 18px;
    height: 16px;
    min-width: 18px;
    margin: 0 1px 0 1px;
    padding: 0;
    border-width: 0;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}

/* NOTE: the hover and pressed fills are set INLINE from WidgetPalette, not here. Both are skin-relative
   washes (WidgetPalette.Ink), and inventing a --sasq-hover-wash token for one control would have to be
   mirrored in both theme sheets forever — TestThemeTokenSheetParity enforces exactly that, and caught the
   first attempt. Same reasoning, same place, as the Script Header bar right above this feature. */

/* Group divider. Navigation | readout | actions — the grouping is the whole reason the row scans as three
   jobs instead of eight loose buttons. */
.sasq-debug-transport__sep {
    width: 1px;
    height: 12px;
    margin: 0 4px 0 4px;
    background-color: var(--sasq-border, #3f3f3f);
}

.sasq-debug-transport__readout {
    -unity-font-style: normal;
}

/* LIVE and TIPS. A rounded chip reads as a state light as well as a button, which is what both of these are:
   LIVE says "these numbers are current" and un-freezes the playhead; TIPS says "field tooltips are on" and
   turns them off. Unity's own Toggle is a checkbox plus a label — around 60px on a bar that already wraps at
   198px, and drawn in the editor skin rather than this one.

   Colours are set INLINE from WidgetPalette (see Paint), for the same reason the button hover washes are:
   they are skin-relative, and a --sasq-* token invented for one control has to be mirrored in both theme
   sheets forever. Geometry only, here. */
.sasq-debug-transport__pill {
    height: 14px;
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0 2px 0 2px;
    padding: 0 5px 0 5px;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-radius: 7px;
    font-size: 8px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
}

/* The row the jump-to-change buttons are scoped to. Without a tell, "next change" silently means something
   different depending on which graph you last touched — the same class of quiet lie the old global search was,
   arriving from the other direction. */
.sasq-debug-row--focused .sasq-debug-well {
    border-color: var(--sasq-accent, #2f7ad4);
}
